# work_router (2026-11-22): the in-house router (tool_score_op over harness_bank_op) sends a goal in words to one of 20 WORK-INTENT entries in harness/bank-work/ (a repeated job of mine -> the real command or doc).
# Matching is WHOLE WORD, exact: a multi-word keyword never matches, every query word found in a SENTENCE adds 0.25, so the caller drops stopwords (the word lists below are already filtered).
# Measured 2026-11-22: DEV set (20 goals, tuned against) 18/20; HELD-OUT set (20 goals written in new words, run once) 18/20 = 90%. This case asserts only the goals that route RIGHT today; the known misses are listed below, NOT asserted:
#   KNOWN-MISS dev: "run the chain signed test" -> chain_wallet (words chain, signed are chain keywords); "new test that can fail for the sender check" -> run_harness_case
#   KNOWN-MISS held-out: "add coverage that fails when the sender id is not validated" -> run_harness_case; "enter text into the composer by injecting key presses" -> launch_hai_cli (composer is its keyword)
# CAVEAT: tool_score_op said FIRE on every goal, wrong ones too: RULE tool_fire_min alone does not separate right from wrong (first-to-second score gap does, partly). A margin rule is the next step (a change to the shared op, owner/stronger-agent review).
# Needs the compiled tool_score_op and harness_bank_op (ops/+x). No network, no shell.
RESULTS | ../results/work_router.txt
ENV | LC_ALL | C

CASE | routes-that-are-right-today
